mphocytes (Less likely due to blasts instead of atypical lymphocytes and pancytopenia pattern)", "Metastatic Visceral Mass Syndrome (Less likely due to lack of focal neurological deficits beyond mild ataxia)"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional alarm signs (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Hematological red flags (blasts on CBC, pancytopenia)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.6784615384615386, "posterior": 0.320609220597654, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Lack of lymphoid morphology directly supports myeloid over lymphoid origins, reinforcing B1 and weakening B2."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.145, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of lymphoid morphology directly supports myeloid over lymphoid origins, reinforcing B1 and weakening B2."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.11307692307692309, "posterior": 0.3798808226619894, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The subacute course and no chronic disease history slightly favors chronic processes but lacks sufficient specificity to change B1's dominance."], "evidence_against": ["The absence of chronic CML history combined with subacute presentation moderately